    "explanation": "To both parties, on trip TRP-09111.\n\nTHE DEVIATION IS ESTABLISHED. The governing figure is gps_trace.trace_distance_km (EV-GPS-09111): 16.2 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff against a booked optimal of 12.0 km (EV-TRIP-09111) — an excess of 4.2 km, or 35% of optimal. That clears both POL-RD-01 gates (more than 20% and more than 0.8 km). It reaches neither materiality gate (more than 50% or more than 8.0 km), so POL-RD-06 is not engaged: no driver-profile test, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral arise from this trip. I make no adverse use of either profile (POL-GEN-01).\n\nNO EXCULPATION APPLIES. (1) The driver's account, 'I followed the road available to me', is a general assertion that cites no evidence. Under POL-RD-08 the driver must point to a specific artifact and a specific clause to invoke an exculpatory clause, and a general assertion unsupported by a traffic-advisory ID does not discharge that burden; it carries no weight and is discarded. POL-RD-03 was therefore not invoked against a cited artifact, and the mandatory-escalation ground in POL-RD-10(5) is NOT engaged. The only advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-09111-01, is MISSING — no payload, weight_multiplier 0.0, code MISSING_ARTIFACT — which is citable as the absence of any advisory, but absence of the artifact a clause would need is not the same as a clause invoked against a cited absent artifact, and an uncited denial does not manufacture an escalation. (2) The chat log (EV-CHAT-09111) shows the rider asking to rejoin the booked route and the driver declining; there was no rider-requested detour (POL-RD-04). (3) No endpoint was amended (POL-RD-05). (4) The trip is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL (POL-RD-12). (5) The fare is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not close off the distance-and-time refund.\n\nTHE REFUND IS ARITHMETIC (POL-RD-02). Charged total from EV-FARE-09111: SGD 33.36. Recomputed fare: ((3.80 + 0.75 x 12.0 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.2 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 1.00 ERP on the optimal route − 1.00 promo discount = SGD 24.224. Refund = 33.36 − 24.224 = SGD 9.136, payable rounded up to SGD 9.15. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, and below 90% of the charged total, so the outcome is a partial refund.\n\nTHE ERP POINT. The SGD 2.00 'Tuas South Avenue 8 loop' gantry (on_optimal_route false) is already comprehended in the recomputed fare, which credits only the SGD 1.00 on-optimal-route gantry; under POL-RD-09(1) it is itemised for transparency and is NOT added on top of the SGD 9.15. It is not a phantom line — the vehicle crossed it on the detour — so no billing-integrity referral arises.\n\nCONFIDENCE. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact (trip record, GPS trace, fare breakdown, chat log) has weight_multiplier 1.0, so the cap under POL-GEN-02(2) is 1.0; the missing advisory carries no deciding fact and does not move the cap. Confidence is recorded at 0.90.",
